  "native_scope": "Seven original functions: supplied-manager setup, global preference and explicit fallback for direct component calls, first-fit allocation, alignment, minimum and split thresholds, valid-owned free/coalescing, NULL and failed allocations, lock stores/getter, complete guarded buffers and globals, three consistent pointer aliases, signed cleanup counts, original release order, external and pooled owners, fragmented pools, repeated cleanup, o32 saved registers, stack and red zones. The entire native cleanup/free/lock graph runs uninterrupted without output stubs. The caller teardown is separate. Invalid/duplicate frees, overflowing requests, OS allocator failure, concurrent execution, physical cards, natural error-path reachability, PS1 timing, padding-source recovery and whole-feature parity are not established.",
